From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 13:10:36 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] windows.applicationmodel.useractivities: Give a desktop
 application a request manager for each of its windows.

Word asks the factory of UserActivityRequestManager for
IUserActivityRequestManagerInterop when it opens a document and gets
its manager for the document window from GetForWindow; Wine had only
GetForCurrentView.  As tools/useractivityprobe in the outer tree
measured on Windows, a window of the process gets a manager, the same
one while it is held and another for another window, a child window
included; no window or one that is gone gives
ERROR_INVALID_WINDOW_HANDLE and a window of another process, the
desktop's too, E_ACCESSDENIED.  A desktop application has no current
view, so GetForCurrentView now fails with ERROR_NOT_FOUND as it does
there instead of making a manager.  The managers are not agile, and
the token for a handler is its address.

The declarations are in a new useractivityinterop.idl, as in the
Windows SDK.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 06d5d17829962331140c0dfa60aeec983313e78f)

